commit d2f590d28247dd751bf5c413d94625271ae394a4
Author:     GEEKiDoS <geek_ds@foxmail.com>
AuthorDate: Sun Sep 27 01:13:19 2026 +0800
Commit:     bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>
CommitDate: Sun Sep 27 16:25:29 2026 +0800

    BACKPORT-ELDEN: wifi/bt/pwrseq: Peach v2 (WCN7861) support from the Lenovo Y700 Gen4 port
    
    Extracted from GEEKiDoS/linux v7.2-elden commit b0c05eb72e10 ("arm64:
    qcom: add Lenovo Legion Tab Y700 Gen4 support"), SM8750 with the same
    Peach v2 / Brahma combo as piano. Only the connectivity parts are taken:
    
    - ath12k: ATH12K_HW_PEACH_HW20 (QCC2072-class HAL, 0x3278 BAR window,
      cnss2 32-vector MSI layout), TME-L patch, OL-CPR PMU parameters
      forwarded to the power sequencer, QDSS config, board API 1 only.
    - pwrseq-qcom-wcn: qcom,wcn7861-pmu with AOSS-QMP PDC init tables and
      OL-CPR voltage votes; pci-pwrctrl-pwrseq: pci17cb,110e.
    - btqca/hci_qca: qcom,wcn7861-bt; for Peach v2 ROM tuples skip the 0xfc48
      baud change like the stock HAL and pace unacked TLV segments.
    - pcie-qcom/qmp-pcie: iommu-map parsing with #iommu-cells = 2, keep the
      PHY/controller power domains in the wakeup path.
    
    Conflict in pci-pwrctrl-pwrseq.c resolved against the piano 110e entry;
    the earlier piano routing of 0x110e through the WCN7850 probe path is
    dropped in favour of the dedicated Peach case.
    
    Signed-off-by: GEEKiDoS <geek_ds@foxmail.com>
    [piano: extracted subset, conflict resolution]

